   152	This is **not** a valid kill, and the reason is exactly the FALLACY-v2
   153	carrier/attainment separation. `corr_l` is a sum of **local multiplicity
   154	jumps** `μ_x − μ_l`, and `μ_x` is the local degree of `f^*` at `x` in the sense
   155	of [R3] — the number of nearby points with a common image. Ramification of `h_l`
   156	controls only the part `μ_l(s_l − 1)` coming from the collision of `e_t` sheets
   157	of the *parametrization*; the residue `k_t = μ_t − e_t μ_l` counts preimages
   158	supplied by the *surface* germ at `x` (affine branches escaping to infinity
   159	along the contracted configuration), and nothing in Riemann–Hurwitz bounds it.
   160	Indeed a jump of `μ_t = 10` at a point with `e_t = 2`, `μ_l = 2` is not
   161	contradicted by any ramification count: `k_t = 6` is a fibre-budget quantity,
   162	governed by [P7], not by RH.
   163	
   164	So the arithmetic route the charge names is genuinely blocked. The correct
   165	attack is not "how many units fit on the ramification divisor" but **"how many
   166	distinct sites can carry a jump at all"** — and the answer, from Orevkov's own
   167	§2–§4, is one per dicritical.
   168	
   169	## 3. The pointwise dictionary [Z-6.5b], re-derived
   170	
   171	Fix the notation of [R1]/[R3]. `X̃` is the regularizing blow-up, `L = X̃ − C̃²`
   172	its boundary (a tree of nonsingular rational curves, pairwise transversal),
   173	`L_∞ = f^{-1}(P¹×P¹ − C²)`, `L_FC = L − L_∞`, `L_C ⊂ L_FC` the contracted
   174	components, `L_F = L_FC − L_C` the affine-image dicriticals. For a dicritical
   175	`l ⊂ L_F` in the chain `K : l_1 — ⋯ — l_k` of [R1], `l = l_k`, and
   176	
   177	```text
   178	l′ := l ∩ f^{-1}(C²) = l_k − {p} ≅ A¹        ( [R1](a),(b) )
   179	```
   180	
   181	where `p = K ∩ L_∞` is the unique boundary meeting point. Write `φ_l = f|_{l′}`,
