   247	
   248	## 4. Riemann–Hurwitz for `h_l` and the total-ramification normal form
   249	
   250	> **Theorem 4.A (rigidity of the correction carrier).** Assume H2, and assume
   251	> some dicritical has `μ_0 = 1` (so [P5] holds: `D̃ ≅ A¹`, `η` immersive). Let
   252	> `l` be an affine-image dicritical. Then exactly one of:
   253	>
   254	> 1. `s_l = 1` (`h_l` an isomorphism) and `corr_l = 0`; or
   255	> 2. `s_l ≥ 2`, `μ_l ≥ 2`, `l` carries a nonempty `L_C` chain, and, after affine
   256	>    coordinate choices on `l′ ≅ A¹` and `D̃ ≅ A¹`,
   257	>    ```text
   258	>    h_l(t) = (t − t_0)^{s_l},
   259	>    ```
   260	>    i.e. `h_l` is **totally ramified at the single point** `t_0 = l ∩ L_C`,
