   294	because `η` is immersive. A one-line expansion gives
   295	
   296	```text
   297	Jac(X,Y) = v^{μ−1}·G,    G = μ X_u B + v (X_u B_v − X_v B_u).
   298	```
   299	
   300	Since `f^*(dx∧dy) = dX_1∧dX_2` on `C̃²` (Keller), `div(Jac)` in this chart is
   301	effective and supported on `L ∩ U = {v=0}`, so `G = v^m·G̃` with `G̃(t) ≠ 0` and
   302	`m ≥ 0`. If `m ≥ 1` then `G|_{v=0} = μ X_u(u,0)B(u,0) ≡ 0`, forcing `v | B`, a
   303	contradiction. So `m = 0`, i.e. `μ X_u(0,0)B(0,0) ≠ 0`, i.e. `X_u(0,0) ≠ 0`,
   304	i.e. `e = 1`. The toy map `(u,v) ↦ (u², v²)` shows the mechanism is sharp: it
