   386	attainment claim.
   387	
   388	**(f) `q′ = 1` is impossible.** With `q′ = 1`, (5.1) reads `W + d − 1 ≤ d`,
   389	i.e. `W ≤ 1`. But `W ≥ b + 4q′ ≥ 5`. So **any surviving configuration has at
   390	least two distinct correction carriers**, hence (by 5.2) `W ≥ 9`.
   391	
   392	This single line is the whole kill of the N=20 packet, and is the structural
   393	statement to remember: a lone ramified carrier can never balance the excess
   394	budget, because it offers only one site and each site is capped at `d`.
   395	
   396	## 6. Re-running the N=20 budget: packet (4.9) is dead
   397	
   398	Packet (4.9) has `b = 1`, `q = 1`, one carrier `(μ, s, corr) = (2, 3, 16)`,
   399	`W = 7`, `d = 6`, `a = 13`, `N = 20`. Hence `q′ = 1`.
   400	
   401	**Kill, form 1 (via §5(f)).** `q′ = 1` gives `W + d − 1 ≤ d`, i.e. `7 + 6 − 1 = 12 ≤ 6`.
   402	False. **Packet (4.9) is refuted.**
   403	
   404	**Kill, form 2 (explicit, so the mechanism is visible).** By Theorem 4.A the
   405	cubic `h_1` is totally ramified: `h_1(t) = (t − t_0)³`, one critical point
