   411	k_1 = μ_{x_0} f^* − e_{t_0} μ_1 = 18 − 3·2 = 12.
   412	```
   413	
   414	All 12 units of excess sit over the single physical point `p`, so `K_p = 12`.
   415	By §5(b), `p ∈ Sing D` and `r_p ≥ 2`; [P7] then gives
   416	
   417	```text
   418	a_p = N − r_p W − K_p ≤ 20 − 2·7 − 12 = −6 < 0,
   419	```
   420	
   421	which is absurd (`a_p` is a cardinality). Equivalently `K_p ≤ d = 6` while the
   422	concentration theorem demands `K_p = 12`. Even the most generous reading
