   424	`a_p = 20 − 7 − 12 = 1 ≥ 0`, so the packet is not killed by fibre positivity
   425	alone; it is killed by `r_p ≥ 2`, which rests on [P5] (branches smooth,
   426	singularities multibranch) plus [P6] (smooth-stratum covering). Both are
   427	promoted and both are already load-bearing for the promoted `N ≥ 20` frontier,
   428	so no new hypothesis is imported here.
   429	
   430	**No neighbouring `N = 20` shape survives.** REV §4.4–§4.5 enumerated the `W=7`
   431	shapes: `(1,1) + (2,3)` — just killed — and `(1,1) + (3,2)`, which has `q′ = 1`
   432	and dies by §5(f) as well (it already died under the weaker `R = 1` bound). Any
   433	`N = 20` shape needs `2W + d = 20` with `d ≥ 1`, so `W ≤ 9`; and `q′ ≥ 2`
   434	requires `W ≥ 9`, forcing `W = 9`, `d = 2`, `q′ = 2`, and then (5.1) reads
   435	`9 + 2 − 1 = 10 ≤ 2·2 = 4`, false. So:
   436	
   437	> **No configuration at `N = 20` survives.** The first escape does not occur
   438	> at degree 20.
   439	
   440	**The same sweep excludes every `N ≤ 25`.** Substituting `W = 4q′ + 1 + ε`
   441	(`ε ≥ 0`) and `N = 2W + d` into (5.1) with `q′ ≥ 2`:
   442	
   443	```text
   444	(q′ − 1) d ≥ W − 1 ≥ 4q′   ⟹   d ≥ 4q′/(q′ − 1),
   445	N = 2W + d ≥ 2(4q′ + 1) + ⌈4q′/(q′ − 1)⌉ = 8q′ + 2 + ⌈4q′/(q′−1)⌉.
   446	```
   447	
   448	| `q′` | min `W` | min `d` | min `N` |
   449	|---:|---:|---:|---:|
   450	| 1 | — | impossible | — |

