1. A.G. Vitushkin, On polynomial transformations of Cn , Manifolds-Tokyo 1973, Univ. of Tokyo
   Press, Tokyo, 1975, pp. 415–417.
2. H. Bass, E.H. Connell, D. Wright, The Jacobian Conjecture: Reduction of degree and formal
   expansion of the inverse, Bull. Amer. Math. Soc. (N. S.) 7 (1982), 287–330.
3. A.G. Vitushkin, Some examples in connection with problems about polynomial transforma-
   tions of C2 , Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR, Ser. Mat. 35 (1971), 269–279 (in Russian); English
   transl., Math. USSR-Izv. 5 (1971), 278–288.
4. S. Lojasiewicz, Triangulation of semi-analytic sets, Ann. Scuola Norm. Sup. Pisa (3) 18
   (1964), 449–474.
5. D. Mumford, The topology of normal singularities of an algebraic surface and a criterion for
   simplicity, Publ. Math. I.H.E.S. 9 (1961), 5–22.
6. J. Milnor, Singular points of complex hypersurfaces, Ann. Math. Studies, no. 61, Princeton
   Univ. Press, Princeton, 1968.
7. O. Zariski, On the topology of algebroid singularities, Amer. J. Math. 54 (1932), 453–465.
8. S. Abhyankar, T.-T. Moh, Embeddings of the line in the plane, J. Reine Angew. Math. 276
   (1975), 148–166.

